# stacks/ is config-as-code: ONLY the compose definition, scrubbed env examples,
# and docs are tracked. Everything a running stack writes under its dir
# (bind-mounted config/data/state/secrets — e.g. arr-stack/{radarr,sonarr,…},
# homeassistant/config, matter-server/data, openclaw/{config,workspace,auth-secrets})
# is ignored by default, so no state or secret can be committed by accident.
*
!*/
!.gitignore
!README.md
!*/README.md
!*/docker-compose.yml
!*/*.env.example
